{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/466750-wanted-to-read-up-on-copyrights-for-white-wolf","id":466750,"title":"Wanted to read up on Copyrights for White Wolf","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-02T18:03:22-07:00","id":466750,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Wanted to read up on Copyrights for White Wolf","content":"Hi everybody!<br /> So I've been working on my own system for a genre of tabletop game that's utterly unrelated to anything I've seen by white wolf, with the exception that so far I've looked at using D10's for the dice mechanic. However... I don't want to, well, infringe upon any copyrights. I've been looking at what is copyrighted and that's the Storyteller and Storytelling systems, which is somewhat vague. I was wondering if anyone knew any more about specifically what you should be avoiding.<br /> <br /> I assume that the use of a D10 as a dice mechanic is generally open-content since its... well, a die. But I've been wrong before and if I learned anything from Palladiumbooks, Some developers get really touchy about what they consider 'their property'.<br /> <br /> I also would like to know if the clumping of three sets of stats and then three sets of skills is something that's too much like their systems.<br /> <br /> In case there is concerns, what I'm working on is in every way other than the two things I'm asking about above really different. So I'm not trying to make a knockoff system or a clone; I mean if it was that similar I'd just make it a houseruled version of their system and only share it with friends.<br /> <br /> Anywho, I'd appreciate something about the above. Mainly I am checking because I want to prevent there from being problems in the future. Not that I'm expecting for what I'm working on to *take off* and become popular enough it would actually HARM any of the company's sales, but rather just because it's the polite thing to do.<br /> <br /> Thanks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1401-rungok","name":"rungok","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1401_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T19:32:17-07:00","id":466886,"title":"","content":"IANAL:<br /> <br /> The general wisdom one RPG copyrights is the following. Mechanics cannot be copyrighted. Only the fashion in which they're presented can be.<br /> <br /> If you want to make a system where you form a dice-pool of D10s based on the sum of two traits, you just have to make sure it is distinct enough from the ST systems; not just a reskin of them.<br /> <br /> Here's a decent test you can do. You can download the Revised Dark Ages Revised core rules for free* from DrivethruRPG.com if you need a document to compare to. Can someone run your game using a core ST system document replacing your core rules? Does your game work as a fan-supplement to those core rules? If so, you're probably not changing enough. If you'd need a third document just to translate between the two? You're pretty solid.<br /> <br /> Another option is to finish your system and send it to CCP (as they are the copyright owners) to ask how they feel about any similarities between your product and their properties.<br /> <br /> * - DA Revised Core rule set was released after WW released it was kind of unfair to have none of the other DA Revised games get the core rules and force Werewolf/Mage/Fae/Inquisition fans to buy a Vampire book just for the central rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-18T20:38:56-07:00","id":485038,"title":"","content":"Ah i see!<br /> <br /> Hmm... I will compare and report back what I find out. I have been trying pretty hard to make a system with a good depth to complexity ratio, so I hope it is different enough to not be a problem at all.<br /> <br /> What ypu had to say was informative though. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1401-rungok","name":"rungok","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1401_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T08:18:45-07:00","id":485424,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Sorry, but we can't have discussions involving legal advice on the forums.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}